{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Well I [A]taught that weeping willow how to [A]cry cry cry,
[A]Taught the clouds how to cover up a [B]clear blue sky.[E]
[A]And the tears I cried [A7]for that woman [D]are gonna flood [D7]you big river,
And [A]I'm a gonna sit right [E7]here until I [A]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I met her accidentally in St. Paul, Minnesota,
It tore me up everytime I heard her drawl, That southern drawl.
Well I heard my dream went back downstream, Cavortin' in Davenport,
And I followed you big river, when you called.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Well I followed her down to St. Louis, Later on down the river,
A freighter said she's been here, But she's gone, boy, she's gone.
I followed her down to Memphis, But she just walked off the bus,
She raised a few eyebrows and she went on down alone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Well I've gotten on down to Baton Rouge, River Queen roll on,
Take that woman down to New Orleans, New Orleans.
I give up, I've had enough, Followed my blues on down to the gulf,
She loves you big river more than me.
{end_of_verse}
